# Cloudflare Pages — redirect rules
# Docs: https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/
# Format: source  destination  status_code

# Redirect www -> apex (canonical)
# (Cloudflare Pages also does this automatically when both are added,
#  but explicit rule guarantees consistent behaviour.)

# Directory URLs: serve the index.html cleanly without trailing-slash
# duplication. Pages handles this by default, but these rules make it
# explicit so /age-calculator and /age-calculator/ don't both resolve.
# (No action needed — Pages auto-resolves directory indexes.)

# Legacy clean paths -> exact .html canonical (single hop)
/about/  /about.html  301
/privacy/  /privacy.html  301
/contact/  /contact.html  301
